SUMMARY
==============================================================================================================
  A cap built from the MOND-sector field alone keeps the carrier exactly Newtonian with the gate varied (A1).  The cap
  must read the mean curvature of the MOND field's equipotentials, kappa_X = (1/2) div(grad Phi_X/|grad Phi_X|), which is
  1/r for every spherical profile (A2): U_cap = C min(lap Phi_X, v_cap^2 kappa_X^2) ends every spherical region at
  l_cap(z) = v_cap/(H sqrt(x_c)) = 1.75 Mpc at z = 0.5 and 2.99 Mpc at z = 0.023, and reproduces MS3's pass
  (1.418/1.567).  L395's form, lap Phi_X/|grad Phi_X|, is (1 + beta_b/2)/r: on baryons that keep
  tracing a cluster past r200 its edge sits 1.27x further out at 1e14.5 and cosmic shear fails
  (1.418/1.567).  The fourth-order term of the capped gate keeps a sign change inside
  the transition layer (P1): DE7's repair is still needed.  v_cap = 325 km/s stays a declared constant.

